# HELD migrations — files that exist on trunk but MUST NOT be applied to production yet.
# One filename per line. `scripts/deploy-migrations.sh` moves every file listed here aside before
# it runs `supabase db push`, so a held file can never ship as cargo on someone else's deploy.
#
# A line here is a decision by the migration's owner, recorded in REGISTRY.md. Remove the line in the
# same commit that lands the file (or supersedes it) — and say why in the REGISTRY row.
#
# History: 2026-08-19 — trunk's 0105 was reviewer-rejected (docs/security-booking-party-forgery.md)
# and kept out of every deploy by hand ("mv 0105 aside"). The same day, catalog measured that
# `db push --include-all` from any tree carrying it lists 0105 to push. Five hand-steps became this
# file plus a script.
#
# 2026-08-19 (evening): the 0105 line is GONE — the file was SUPERSEDED and deleted by
# `0111_booking_entry_rebuild.sql` in the same commit (REGISTRY rows 0105 and 0111). Removing it
# here in that same commit is the rule three lines up, and skipping it would make
# `scripts/deploy-migrations.sh` print `warning: HELD names 0105… but trunk has no such file
# (stale line?)` on EVERY future deploy — a warning that fires every time is a warning nobody reads.
# This file is now empty of entries, which is the state it is supposed to spend most of its life in.
